{"nelson":{"id":"d5f3f25d-322f-421d-a117-5f5a345d85d3","word":"Nelson","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"male given name","tags":["masculine"],"word":"Nélson"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"categories":["English surnames","English surnames from patronymics"],"links":[["surname","surname"]],"glosses":["A surname originating as a patronymic."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"29e1ba6f-0311-41a3-80e5-74e968f8ce8c"},{"examples":[{"text":"Africans of my generation - and even today - generally have both a Western and an African name. Whites were either unable or unwilling to pronounce an African name, and considered it uncivilized to have one. That day, Miss Mdingane told me that my new name was Nelson. Why she bestowed this particular name upon me I have no idea. Perhaps it had something to do with the great British sea captain Lord Nelson, but that would only be a guess.","ref":"1994, Nelson Mandela, Long Walk to Freedom:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[261,267],[402,408]],"id":"680b9afd-77b9-42c6-8cfa-b55b7b20e4a4"}],"categories":["English given names","English male given names","English male given names from surnames","English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"links":[["given name","given name"]],"glosses":["A male given name transferred from the surname."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"706b7902-6995-4278-a168-1ad510ec61f3"},{"links":[["placename","placename"],["Australia","Australia#English"],["suburb","suburb"],["Sydney","Sydney#English"],["New South Wales","New South Wales#English"],["Australia","Australia#English"]],"glosses":["A placename","A place in Australia.","A suburb of Sydney, New South Wales, Australia."],"categories":["en:Places in Australia","en:Places in New South Wales, Australia","en:Places in Sydney","en:Suburbs of Sydney"],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"0d1664e3-aae2-4bc9-b9d4-ba1cef57a229"},{"links":[["placename","placename"],["Australia","A